  "title": "Advanced Video Gen & Agent Model Control",
  "summary": "Vertex AI introduces LoRA and Super Resolution configurations for large vision model video generation experiments. Agents can now specify a default model and temperature, and evaluation runs gain cross-region model flexibility.",
  "details": "Developers can now fine-tune video generation experiments using new LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation) configurations via `CloudAiLargeModelsVisionGenerateVideoExperiments.loraConfig`. This includes specifying multiple `adapters` with `id` and `weight`. Additionally, `superResConfig` allows for Pro Super Resolution upsampling with modes like `MODE_4K` and `MODE_8K`. For Vertex AI Agents, the new `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Agent.modelConfig` property enables setting a default `model` and `temperature` for the agent's tasks. Finally, `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfig` now includes `allowCrossRegionModel` to permit evaluation runs to utilize models across different regions.",
